From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Anforowicz <lukasza@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:21:53 -0700
Subject: [orb] Add `text/pdf` to the `opaque-blocklisted-never-sniffed` list.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ORB already protects `application/pdf` so this should be a reasonable
change. It should have no web-visible change in behavior, except if
images/video/etc are labeled as `text/pdf` (which seems unlikely in
practice).

This CL can be seen as a follow-up to https://crbug.com/40774340 which
implemented support for recognizing `text/pdf` as a PDF document.
https://github.com/annevk/orb/pull/46 corresponds to this change.

Fixed: 560039872
Bug: 40774340
Change-Id: I09505eddfea8a85944cc3e6f7dcfd83f7efb5507
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8400027
Reviewed-by: Charlie Reis <creis@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Łukasz Anforowicz <lukasza@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Łukasz Anforowicz <lukasza@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1696707}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
